Z||000000||olympic||03-04-2000||05:57 PM||||Has anyone here joined this and have you made any money?? Everyone around my town is talking about it.  I personnally think it's a scam and the police have been all over the radio saying it's illegal under Canadian law.<BR>   <BR>    If you haven't heard about this it goes something like this.   You buy a 15 meg website under the skynary domain name for $100US.  Then you get 2 other people to buy a website and those two people get 2 other people each to buy a site.(tell me how this is not a pyramid scheme?)  You get paid for everyone who joins skybiz under you in your pyramid through to infinity, not just 3 or 4 levels below you.  They pay about $420US for every 50 signups in your pyramid.<P>My question is, who in their right mind would pay $100US PER YEAR for a puny 15 meg site when you can get a bigger, free site anywhere else.  You don't even get your own domain name here!!!  I think they are just preying on people who don't know much about the internet. And I'll bet my last dollar that the man at the very top of this giant pyramid is the president of skybiz 2000 himself.  Not only is he making a fortune selling $100 per year websites but he's also pocketing $400 for every 50 suckers that buy into this!!||||reg||1
